  "slug": "learning-causation-2f3a",
  "summary": "Recent benchmarks and new Bayesian, bootstrap and integrative approaches address inference validity under compositionality and confounding.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is statistical methodology for microbiome data, where compositional structure and confounding complicate inference. PGL applies Bayesian multinomial logit-normal shrinkage with phylogenetic borrowing to ASV-level feature selection. A benchmark of 71 single-cohort and 63 multi-cohort confounder-aware differential abundance strategies, with xConDA released, assesses methods via simulations and real data. A high-dimensional structural equation framework integrates large microbiome cohorts with smaller paired microbiome-metabolome data to construct disease pathways. Outside microbiome data, ssGSEA3.0 replaces feature-label permutation with feature-level bootstrap resampling for per-sample significance, and a 12-method differential composition benchmark on population-scale single-cell data uses real data, permutations and simulations. The shared element is explicit attention to uncertainty and validation, though the items differ in analytical aim.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-05"
}
